      "Language": "ukr",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Results of operative treatment of 136 patients in 2005-2015 yrs, suffering gastroesophageal reflux disease, are presented. Basing on the deepened comparative analysis of the early postoperative period course peculiarities, the efficacy and lesser traumaticity of miniinvasuve intervention was proved, concerning lesser duration of pulmonary artificial ventilation, lesser doses of preparations for narcosis, a systolic arterial pressure normalization, as well as the respiration rate up to 12 h postoperatively, lesser intensity of pain (in accordance to the visual analogue scale), lesser doses and quantity of application of narcotic analgetics, early restoration of intestinal peristalsis and the patients activity."},
